Fillets: a blend rolling on an edge whose other contact crosses onto the
face of the spine's next edge goes on along it; that face is no face at
the end (mitcad#343).

The case: a notch wall, a strip narrower than the radius, rounded along
its edges with an earlier rounding R and, past their common vertex, with
a cone; R is tangent to the cone along an edge that runs to the spine's
vertex between the two edges. The ball touches R and rolls on the wall's
far edge; where its contact on R reaches R's edge with the cone, that edge's
face beyond (the cone) holds the spine's end vertex, as the face of the
spine's second edge does. The walk then took the cone for the face at the
end and stopped (ObstacleAtSpineEnd), with most of the spine unwalked, and
ChFi3d_ExtendAtSpineEnds extended that piece past the crossing, over the
next one, for the face at the end to cut it.

- ChFi3d_ArcOntoSpineFaces: whether a contact left its face across an arc
  that does not run to the spine's end vertex, onto faces that all border
  edges of the spine. PerformSetOfSurfOnElSpine does not end a walk rolling
  on an obstacle at such a contact.
- ChFi3d_ExtendAtSpineEnds extends a piece only at an arc whose face beyond
  borders no edge of the spine.

Upstream: new.

